.Dd March 2, 2026
.Dt AS 1
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm as
.Nd Substrate assembler driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl 32 | Fl 64
.Op Fl c
.Op Fl g
.Op Fl I Ar dir
.Op Fl D Ar macro Ns Op = Ns Ar value
.Op Fl march Ar cpu
.Op Fl mtune Ar cpu
.Op Fl msyntax Ns = Ns Ar att|intel
.Op Fl W | Fl -warn | Fl -no-warn | Fl -fatal-warnings
.Op Fl al Ns Op = Ns Ar file
.Op Fl -defsym Ar sym=val
.Op Fl -statistics
.Op Fl -target-help
.Op Fl Wa Ar opts
.Op Fl -max-input-bytes Ar n
.Op Fl -max-line-bytes Ar n
.Op Fl -max-token-length Ar n
.Op Fl -max-macro-depth Ar n
.Op Fl -max-include-depth Ar n
.Op Fl o Ar output
.Ar input.s
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
invokes a backend compiler driver
.Pq usually
.Xr gcc 1
in assembler mode and validates the emitted object using
.Xr libelfobj 3 .
The driver selects 32-bit or 64-bit mode, forwards compatible assembler
options, and validates the generated object as ET_REL with expected class and
machine.
.Pp
The executable aliases
.Nm as.x86
and
.Nm as.x64
select default 32-bit and 64-bit modes respectively.
.Pp
The tree also contains staged native assembler frontend/encoder modules for x86
and ARM development/testing. Current normal
.Nm
CLI output flow remains backend-driver based.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--max-token-length"
.It Fl 32 , Fl 64
Select 32-bit or 64-bit mode.
.It Fl c
Accepted for compatibility; output is always an object file.
.It Fl g
Request debug-capable assembly output from the backend.
.It Fl I Ar dir
Add include search path.
.It Fl D Ar macro Ns Op = Ns Ar value
Define preprocessor symbol.
.It Fl march Ar cpu
Select target machine string.
.It Fl mtune Ar cpu
Select tuning target string.
.It Fl msyntax Ns = Ns Ar att|intel
Select x86 syntax mode.
.It Fl W , Fl -warn
Enable warnings.
.It Fl -no-warn
Disable warnings.
.It Fl -fatal-warnings
Treat warnings as errors.
.It Fl al Ns Op = Ns Ar file
Emit listing output. If
.Ar file
is omitted, output path defaults to
.Ar output
with
.Pa .lst
suffix.
.It Fl -defsym Ar sym=val
Define an absolute assembler symbol.
.It Fl -statistics
Print wall-clock/resource usage statistics.
.It Fl -target-help
Print target summary and exit.
.It Fl Wa Ar opts
Pass comma-separated options to backend assembler.
.It Fl -max-input-bytes Ar n
Reject input larger than
.Ar n
bytes.
.It Fl -max-line-bytes Ar n
Reject logical lines longer than
.Ar n
bytes.
.It Fl -max-token-length Ar n
Reject tokens longer than
.Ar n
bytes.
.It Fl -max-macro-depth Ar n
Reject macro nesting deeper than
.Ar n .
.It Fl -max-include-depth Ar n
Reject include nesting deeper than
.Ar n .
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width AS_BACKEND
.It Ev AS_BACKEND
Path/name of backend compiler driver executable. If unset,
.Nm
uses
.Ev CC
or falls back to
.Dq gcc .
.It Ev AS_ERROR_CODES
If set to a non-empty value,
.Nm
prefixes driver-originated diagnostics with a stable internal error code.
.It Ev AS_MAX_INPUT_BYTES
Default value for
.Fl -max-input-bytes .
.It Ev AS_MAX_LINE_BYTES
Default value for
.Fl -max-line-bytes .
.It Ev AS_MAX_TOKEN_LENGTH
Default value for
.Fl -max-token-length .
.It Ev AS_MAX_MACRO_DEPTH
Default value for
.Fl -max-macro-depth .
.It Ev AS_MAX_INCLUDE_DEPTH
Default value for
.Fl -max-include-depth .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width "123"
.It 0
Successful assembly and validation.
.It 1
Backend execution, validation, or internal driver failure.
.It 2
Usage or argument error.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cc 1 ,
.Xr cpp 1 ,
.Xr ld 1 ,
.Xr libelfobj 3
